-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",37,{
[1153]="7002844D\n1\tDefeat Uruk wood-cutters (total: 12)\tThe Uruk wood-cutters who have destroyed the trees in Nan Curunír can be found in the Vale below. Quickbeam has asked you to defeat the Uruk wood-cutters who destroyed the trees in Nan Curunír.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam east of Isengard\tQuickbeam is at his home on the north-eastern slopes above Nan Curunír. You should tell Quickbeam that you have driven away the Uruk wood-cutters for at least a short time.\n",
[1154]="700606EE\n1\tSearch for Tham Lumren\tTham Lumren is in the north-east Angle. You should look for Thalathril at the the Elven camp, Tham Lumren.\n2\tSpeak to the guard\tTham Lumren is in the north-east Angle. Merileg has asked you to bring a report to Tham Lumren, but the way is guarded. You should speak to the guards to gain entry.\n3\tSpeak to Thalathril\tThalathril is near the large tent in the Elven camp. You should speak to Thalathril.\n",
[1155]="700168CA\n1\tCollect narfulz ore (total: 8)\tNarfulz ore can be found at the Crack's Edge in the centre Nud-melek. You should collect Narfulz ore in Nud-melek.\n2\tBring the ore to Svanr\tYou have collected several rare pieces of Ore as a trophy of your adventures in Nud-melek.\n",
[1156]="700515FC\n1\tSample a draught of Fognoggin\tFognoggin ale can be found in tapped barrels in Wistmead. Halinard Bunce has created a nigh-infamous and ever-changing draught of ale known as Fognoggin. You should try his newest recipe.\n2\tExercise, cold water, or a sudden scare might help lessen the effects of the Fognoggin. Who knows what else might help shake it off? You have tried the newest recipe of Fognoggin ale and should try to find a way to shake off its potent haze.\t\n3\tTalk to Halinard Bunce\tHalinard Bunce can be found in Wistmead. You have tried Halinard Bunce's Fognoggin ale and found it to be quite potent. You should return to Halinard Bunce.\n",
[1157]="70048325\n1\tCollect Hauntreek (total: 12)\tHauntreek can be found in the ruins of Nuiharn, west of Haerondir. Collect Hauntreek.\n2\tBurn Hauntreek in Braziers (total: 4)\tPut the Hauntreek you collected in the braziers found around Haerondir that are beginning to burn low. The Hauntreek will cause the fire to burn a strange blue colour.\n3\tDeliver the Hauntreek to Rhadrog in Haerondir\tRhadrog can be found in Haerondir. You should take the additional Hauntreek and deliver it to Rhadrog.\n",
[1158]="7006868A\n1\tEzôti has asked you to find and paint a rock that looks reasonably like a roc egg. Search for a suitable rock outside the Gate of Songs in the north-eastern wall of Umbar Baharbêl.\t\n2\tInspect rocks outside the city beyond the Gate of Songs (2/3)\tYou have inspected some rocks that did not fit the requirement. Inspect one last rock outside the gates of Umbar Baharbêl.\n3\tPaint the rock\tYou have found the perfect sized rock. Now to paint it so it looks like a roc's egg. Paint the rock outside the gates of Umbar Baharbêl.\n4\tPick up the 'egg' outside the north gate of Umbar Baharbêl\tYou have painted a rock to look like a roc's egg. It's time to deliver it back to Ezôti. Deliver the fake roc's egg to Ezôti in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n5\tTalk to Ezôti\tYou have delivered the 'egg' to Ezôti. Report back to Ezôti in the Upper Ward.\n",
[1159]="700173D1\n1\tTalk to Garthar at the Deep Descent\030Collect Blackened Sword-hilt\tGarthar is at the Deep Descent. Garthar may be able to afford you some level of knowledge about the strange hilt you found.\n",
[1160]="70030235\n1\tRetrieve Léofmar's arrows from vicious Fangorn Huorns (total: 8)\tLéofmar's arrows can be found on the vicious Fangorn Huorns nearby. You should retrieve as many of Léofmar's arrows as you can to help him feel less defenceless.\n2\tReturn Léofmar's arrows to him\tLéofmar is where you left him, hiding against a log in the centre of Fangorn's eaves. You should return Léofmar's arrows to him.\n",
[1161]="70030142\n1\tSearch berry-bushes for signs of being picked (total: 8)\tIf the injured man hunted for food, it is likely that he did not look far from the camp. You should search north-east and south-east of the camp for anything edible the Rohirrim man may have found. It is likely he will still be hungry after his failed attempt at setting up camp.\n2\tTalk to Baillas to ask him for help\tBaillas is in Fangorn Forest, hoping for news of an injured man who walked by him. You should find Baillas once more and ask the old Ent for help finding the Rohirrim.\n",
[1162]="7003FC04\n1\tTalk to Ecthel\tEcthel can be found near the entrance of Morlad in north-western Blackroot Vale. Malthellam has asked you to speak to the remaining guards of Morlad in hopes that you will be able to aid them.\n2\tTalk to Belegant\tBelegant can be found on the second tier of Morlad by following the path that runs south-west. Malthellam has asked you to speak to the remaining guards of Morlad in hopes that you will be able to aid them.\n3\tTalk to Landiach\tLandiach can be found outside Lord Duinhir's home at the peak of Morlad. Malthellam has asked you to speak to the remaining guards of Morlad in hopes that you will be able to aid them.\n4\tTalk to Malthellam\tMalthellam can be found near the entrance of Morlad, outside his home. You have spoken to the guards of Morlad, and should now return to Malthellam.\n",
[1163]="700303B2\n1\tCollect Déorun's loaned hammer\030Collect Déorun's loaned hay-fork\030Collect Déorun's loaned lantern\030Collect Déorun's loaned hunting bow\tDéorun's neighbours can be found within Faldham. Déorun has need of the items he has lent to the other people living around Faldham, including Haligmar, Enswith, Thurgyr, and Osin.\n2\tReturn the items to Déorun\tDéorun resides at his home at the southern end of Faldham, just oustide the mead hall. You have collected Déorun's many missing items, and may now return them to the anxious farmer.\n",
[1164]="7000B951\n1\tRescue Tim Strawley and recover his goods\tThe Gauredain make their home in the south-western hills of Tâl Bruinen, south of Eryn Singor. From the wreckage, it appears that perhaps the mysterious Gauredain Nestael mentioned when you first arrived at Echad Candelleth might be responsible for the attack. You should search for their encampment and rescue Tim Strawley, if he still lives, and recover his goods.\n2\tRecover wooden figurines (total: 8)\030Find Tim Strawley\tThe Gauredain make their home in the south-western hills of Tâl Bruinen, south of Eryn Singor. From the wreckage, it appears that perhaps the mysterious Gauredain Nestael mentioned when you first arrived at Echad Candelleth might be responsible for the attack. You should search for their encampment and rescue Tim Strawley, if he still lives, and recover his goods.\n3\tBring Tim Strawley's wooden figurines to Tongannel\tTongannel is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen, north of Echad Gauradan. You have recovered Tim Strawley's wooden figurines from the Gauredain who stole them, but Strawley himself was slain. You should return the goods to Tongannel.\n",
[1165]="70018FFF\n1\tTalk to Glordirith at Imlad Lalaith\tGlordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin. Limhendeth has asked you to ignore whatever request Asmund made of you, and instead to report of his activities to Glordirith in Lothlórien.\n",
[1166]="70019001\n1\tTalk to Glordirith at Imlad Lalaith\tGlordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil on the banks of Anduin. Limhendeth has asked you to ignore whatever request Asmund made of you, and instead to report of his activities to Glordirith in Lothlórien.\n",
[1167]="70019002\n1\tTalk to Glordirith\tGlordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin. Limhendeth has beseeched you to ignore whatever request Asmund made of you, and to instead speak of his dealings with Glordirith.\n",
[1168]="7002F92A\n1\tDefeat Âmbal and collect a trophy from her\tÂmbal's den can be found west of Caddbrand's camp. Caddabrand is hoping that by defeating the infamous matron, Âmbal, that you might gain fame and fortune, along with Caddabrand.\n2\tReturn the trophy to Caddabrand\tCaddabrand's camp lies to the east of Âmbal's den. Caddabrand awaits your return with the trophy at his camp.\n",
[1169]="70041858\n1\tOst Anglebed can be found in north-central Lebennin. Nimithil has asked you to search Ost Anglebed for signs of treachery from within the guard.\t\n2\tTalk to Nimithil\tNimithil can be found in the lowest section of Ost Anglebed with her guards. You have found a few pieces of concerning evidence in Ost Anglebed, and should return to Nimithil.\n",
[1170]="7002C001\n1\tPour the Ent-draught upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives\tThe gardens of the Entwives lie within the cliffs to the south-east of Gnarlstump. Gnarlstump gave you an Ent-draught and asked you to pour it upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives.\n2\tPour the Ent-draught upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives\tThe gardens of the Entwives lie within the cliffs to the south-east of Gnarlstump. Gnarlstump gave you an Ent-draught and asked you to pour it upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives.\n3\tPour the Ent-draught upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives\tThe gardens of the Entwives lie within the cliffs to the south-east of Gnarlstump. Gnarlstump gave you an Ent-draught and asked you to pour it upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives.\n4\tPour the Ent-draught upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives\tThe gardens of the Entwives lie within the cliffs to the south-east of Gnarlstump. Gnarlstump gave you an Ent-draught and asked you to pour it upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives.\n5\tPour the Ent-draught upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives\tThe gardens of the Entwives lie within the cliffs to the south-east of Gnarlstump. Gnarlstump gave you an Ent-draught and asked you to pour it upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives.\n6\tPour the Ent-draught upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives\tThe gardens of the Entwives lie within the cliffs to the south-east of Gnarlstump. Gnarlstump gave you an Ent-draught and asked you to pour it upon the ruined gardens of the Entwives.\n7\tReturn the Ent-draught to Gnarlstump\tGnarlstump is encamped to the north-west of the gardens of the Entwives. You should let Gnarlstump know what you did and did not discover among the gardens.\n",
[1171]="700529E7\n1\tTalk to Baradal to begin the journey\tBaradal is standing by at the Beorning Watchpost between Duskenvale and the Gladden Fields. You should talk to Baradal.\n2\tTravel south with Baradal\tBaradal has asked to travel with you to the village of Arhaim. You should take the road south with Baradal.\n3\tTalk to Baradal\tBaradal has suddenly stopped along the road to Arhaim. You should talk to Baradal.\n4\tDefeat Orc ambushers (total: 5)\tOrcs lie in wait along the road to Arhaim. You should defeat the Orc ambushers.\n5\tTalk to Baradal\tYou can call Baradal to your side with Baradal's summoning horn. You should talk to Baradal.\n6\tContinue to Arhaim\tThe village of Arhaim lies along the road in Duskenvale. You should travel to Duskenvale.\n7\tTalk to Baradal\tYou can call Baradal to your side with Baradal's summoning horn. You should talk to Baradal.\n",
[1172]="7002812B\n1\tFind Golvorn\tThe missing prisoners and the Man who took them might be found somewhere in the Orc-mines. Edhere asked you to seek his missing companions and the Man who took them.\n2\tRelease Golvorn's captives (total: 3)\tGolvorn's captives are in the Orc-mines. You have defeated Golvorn, a strange and powerful Man who claims to have served Saruman in some fashion. What fate he intended for the slaves he took is unknown, but you can at least free them now.\n3\tTalk to Edhere in the Orc-mines\tEdhere is in the Orc-mines. You should return to Edhere and let him know that Golvorn's captives have been freed.\n",
[1173]="70020DB9\n1\tDefeat Tulwulh-gwirod at night\tTulwulh-gwirod can be found at night in a ravine amid many high bluffs to the south-east of Rhus Cornchúthur. Rhus Cornchúthur suggested that you banish the Cuthraul Tulwulh-gwirod to prove that you are not yourself an evil spirit.\n2\tTalk to Rhus Cornchúthur in the Gloomglens\tRhus Cornchúthur awaits your return to the north-west of Tulwulh-gwirod's haunting grounds. You should return to Rhus Cornchúthur with news of your victory.\n",
[1174]="70058CF0\n1\tCollect Gorgar's orders from Orcs at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (total: 8)\tGorgar's orders are often carried by Orcs at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. Sigvith has asked you to collect orders from the Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.\n2\tDeliver the orders to Sigvith\tSigvith can be found near the gates of Mount Gundabad. You have collected a number of orders from the Orcs at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. You should deliver them to Sigvith.\n",
[1175]="70037A20\n1\tExamine remains of herd-animals (total: 8)\tRemains of herd-animals can be found throughout the plains of the eastern Westfold. You should examine the remains of herd-animals to see how much the Wargs have affected the landscape.\n2\tReturn to Winmar\tWinmar is near the road leading north from Grimslade. You should speak with Winmar.\n",
[1176]="7004E4F3\n1\tCollect the weapon crate\tThe Hammerstead weapons have been crated and are ready for delivery. You should collect the weapon crate.\n2\tTalk to Hógur\tHógur is expecting this weapon shipment in Járnfast. You should talk to Hógur.\n",
[1177]="7006C135\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai (total: 12)\030Destroy Ordâkhai siege weapons (total: 4)\tDestroy siege weapons and defeat Ordâkhai.\n2\tFind and defeat Makóto Dôlo\tFind and defeat Makóto Dôlo.\n3\tDefeat Makóto Dôlo\tFind and defeat Makóto Dôlo.\n",
[1178]="7005A5FA\n1\tDestroy bomb caches (total: 8)\tThe Orcs hide bomb caches in the area between Ashmargathâl and Târ-kútoz. Lúka has requested that you safely destroy any caches you find.\n2\tTalk to Lúka\tYou have scoured the area and destroyed all the bomb caches you could find. You should return to Ashmargathâl and give Lúka the update.\n",
[1179]="70062DDC\n1\tTalk to Gangur Farwend west of the town of Herne\tGangur Farwend asked to meet you west of the town of Herne, where he wished to study some of the curious red rocks to be found there.\n2\tCollect chunks of red rock west of Herne (total: 10)\tChunks of red rock can be found among the craggy outcroppings west of the town of Herne.\n3\tBring the chunks of red rock to Gangur Farwend west of Herne\tGangur Farwend is waiting west of Herne for you to show him the chunks of rock you collected.\n",
[1180]="70041367\n1\tSpeak with Aras at Lang Boha\tAras can be found just north of the Haradrim camp, Lang Boha. You should speak with Aras.\n2\tCollect weapons of the enemy (total: 8)\030Burn the provision tents (total: 4)\tLang Boha can be found on the eastern shores of Dor-en-Ernil. Enter Lang Boha and hinder the Corsair forces.\n3\tSummon and confront the Haradrim Captain of Lang Boha\tThe Captain of the Haradrim camp can be found in Lang Boha. Find and confront the Haradrim Captain.\n4\tSpeak with Aras at Lang Boha\tAras can be found just north of the Haradrim camp, Lang Boha. You should speak with Aras.\n",
[1181]="7002EF4F\n1\tDefeat Orcs in the East Wall and collect short arrows (total: 3)\030Defeat Uruks in the East Wall and collect long arrows (total: 3)\tOrcs and Uruks can be found throughout the East Wall, and even the warriors carry quivers of arrows. Wilferth has asked you to defeat Orcs and Uruks throughout the East Wall and to collect arrows from them for him to study.\n2\tBring the arrows to Wilferth for inspection\tWilferth is at the Rohirrim-camp in the East Wall. You have collected several arrows from the Orcs and Uruks in the East Wall and should bring them to Wilferth for study.\n",
[1182]="70017920\n1\tTalk to Techeryn\tTecheryn is often outside The Forsaken Inn, on the western edge of the Lone-lands. You have been told to speak with Techeryn, an Elf who can give you more insight into the interplay between runes and the natural world.\n2\tTalk to Techeryn and travel to Weathertop for her lesson\tTecheryn is outside The Forsaken Inn, on the western edge of the Lone-lands. The Rune-keeper Techeryn has agreed to entangle more mysteries of runes and is waiting to speak with you.\n3\tTalk to Techeryn at The Forsaken Inn\tTecheryn is outside The Forsaken Inn, on the western edge of the Lone-lands. Your experience on Weathertop with Techeryn has taught you some more about the interplay between runes and the natural world. The Elf is waiting to speak with you about the experience.\n",
[1183]="7001D0D6\n1\tPatrol the first point in southern Gathbúrz\030Patrol the second point in southern Gathbúrz\030Patrol the third point in southern Gathbúrz\030Patrol the fourth point in southern Gathbúrz\tThe first point is east of Thangúlhad. The second point is directly to the south-east of Thangúlhad. The third point is further south-east, near the gate of Dol Guldur. The fourth point is directly south of Thangúlhad. You should scout the waypoints of the patrol that Handelen has asked you to undertake and defeat any enemies that you might find there.\n2\tTalk to Handelen at Thangúlhad\tHandelen is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz. You should return to Handelen with the report of your patrol.\n",
[1184]="70068BDC\n1\tFind the hidden store-room\tLabóni has asked you to investigate The Eastern Stores and retrieve his family heirloom. The Eastern Stores can be found on the east side of the Lower Ward in the Cistern.\n2\tFind Khatrâxi, the Raindrop\tYou have found the Eastern Stores. The family heirloom must be hidden within.\n3\tTalk to Labóni\tYou found The Eastern Stores and have obtained Khatrâxi, the Raindrop. You should return to Labóni.\n",
})
